course: dictionary
lesson: 8082
title: The remainder: what is left over
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When you share things equally, sometimes some are left over. That left-over amount is the remainder. Think of 13 sweets shared between 4 friends: each friend gets 3, and 1 sweet is left over. We write this as 13 ÷ 4 = 3 remainder 1.
explain: The remainder is always smaller than the number you divide by. If you share between 4 friends, the remainder can only be 0, 1, 2 or 3. If you ever get a remainder of 4 or more, you can share out one more each.
explain: Remainder has a second meaning too: the rest of something. «The remainder of the cake» is the part of the cake that is still left after people have eaten some. «The remainder of the day» means all the time from now until bedtime.
fact: The remainder is the amount left over when a number cannot be divided exactly.
fact: 13 divided by 4 is 3 with a remainder of 1, because 4 × 3 = 12 and 13 − 12 = 1.
fact: 23 ÷ 5 = 4 r 3, which means 4 with a remainder of 3.
fact: The remainder is always smaller than the number you divide by.
fact: In everyday words, the remainder of something is the rest of it, the part still left.
exercise: What is the remainder when 23 is divided by 5? | 2 | *3 | 4 | 5
exercise: «I ate half the cake, and the remainder was in the box.» What does remainder mean here? | *The rest that was left | The biggest part of the cake | A number that divides exactly | The box
exercise: Which statement about a remainder is always true? | *It is smaller than the number you divide by | It is always bigger than the number you divide by | It is always zero | It is always an even number
test: What is the remainder when 13 is divided by 4? | 0 | 4 | *1 | 2
test: «I will read the remainder of the book on Sunday.» What does remainder mean here? | The first chapter | The cover of the book | A number | *The part still left
exam: What is the remainder when 29 is divided by 6? | 6 | *5 | 1 | 3
